# Comprehensive test of all new features

# --- Arithmetic Expressions ---
A Number named X exists.
X is 5 plus 3.
Print "5 + 3 = " followed by X.

A Number named Y exists.
Y is 10 minus 4.
Print "10 - 4 = " followed by Y.

A Number named Z exists.
Z is 3 times 7.
Print "3 * 7 = " followed by Z.

A Number named W exists.
W is 20 divided by 4.
Print "20 / 4 = " followed by W.

# --- Comparisons ---
A Number named Score exists.
Score is 85.

If Score is greater than or equal to 80:
    Print "Grade: A".
Otherwise if Score is greater than or equal to 70:
    Print "Grade: B".
Otherwise if Score is greater than or equal to 60:
    Print "Grade: C".
Otherwise:
    Print "Grade: F".

# --- Logic operators ---
A Number named A exists.
A is 10.

A Number named B exists.
B is 20.

If A is greater than 5 and B is less than 30:
    Print "Both conditions true".

If A is less than 5 or B is greater than 15:
    Print "At least one condition true".

# --- Equality ---
If Score is equal to 85:
    Print "Score equals 85".

If Score is not equal to 100:
    Print "Score is not 100".

# --- File I/O ---
Write "Hello from Prose file I/O!" to the file "test_output.txt".

A Text named FileContent exists.
Read the file "test_output.txt" into FileContent.
Print "File content: " followed by FileContent.

# --- JSON Parsing ---
A Text named JsonSource exists.
JsonSource is "{\"name\": \"Alice\", \"age\": 30, \"skills\": [\"coding\", \"design\"]}".

A Dictionary named Parsed exists.
Parsed is the parsed JSON of JsonSource.

Print "JSON name: " followed by (the value for "name" inside Parsed).

# --- Try/Catch ---
Try:
    Execute the shell command "nonexistent-command-xyz".
Catch the error into ErrMsg:
    Print "Caught error: " followed by ErrMsg.

Print "Program continues after error handling".
